Anker today launched the <a href="https://eufy-us.sjv.io/5kdOX1">Eufy TrackLight Cam S1</a>, which it says is the world's first outdoor security camera with an auto-tracking light for actively deterring intruders. The TrackLight Cam S1 is compatible with Apple Home when using the Anker HomeBase, so it can be used alongside other smart home devices in a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/homekit/">HomeKit</a> setup.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/eufy-tracklight-camera.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076800" /><br/>
When a suspicious person is detected, the camera locks on and follows them with a light from up to 12 meters (40 feet) away. The light adjusts with distance, narrowing when someone is far away and broadening as they approach. The camera has 355 degrees of horizontal rotation and can track movement up to 87 degrees per second.<br/>
<br/>
An optional tracking deterrence mode activates the light and a 105-decibel siren at the same time, plus there is a red and blue flashing light mode as an additional deterrent.<br/>
<br/>
The camera records in 4K with 10x digital zoom and night vision to show strangers in the dark. There is a 120-degree floodlight that works alongside the TrackLight, and dual radars offer 180-degree detection up to 40 feet. A Family List in the app allows the homeowner to set known people, so they get a soft, welcoming light as they approach. The feature detects a known phone's Bluetooth.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/anker-eufy-tracklight.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076648" /><br/>
There's a 15,000mAh battery and a 5.5-watt solar panel for continuous operation, and IP65 dust and water resistance offers protection from the elements. There is no built-in storage, and users will need to add a microSD card or connect to the HomeBase. No subscription is required.<br/>
<br/>
Anker also recently launched its Window Camera E10, a 2.5K resolution camera with anti-reflection and 25 degrees of tilt. It's designed to be put in a window, covering a yard, driveway, or entry without needing to be outdoors.<br/>
<br/>
